course: dictionary
lesson: 4192
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and goodness is a good example. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means. «Bread fills ducks with little goodness» is about food, so goodness here means the healthy part of food that does you good.
explain: «Goodness!» or «My goodness!» is not about food or behaviour. People say it to show surprise, like «Goodness me!» when something amazes them. Check the sentence: if you can swap in the word surprised and it still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
explain: When goodness means how a person behaves, it means being kind and honest. Stories show it through actions, such as sharing your last sweet or telling the truth when it is hard. Look for the actions, because they are the clues.
fact: Goodness is a noun, and it can also be a short exclamation, as in «Goodness!»
fact: Goodness can mean the quality of being good, kind and honest.
fact: Goodness can mean the healthy part of food that does you good: «A panda gets little goodness from bamboo.»
fact: Phrases like «thank goodness» and «goodness knows» are common, and their meaning comes from the whole phrase.
fact: Goodness is uncountable, so in ordinary use you do not say "a goodness" or "two goodnesses."
exercise: «Bread fills ducks up without much goodness.» In this sentence, goodness means | A duck's favourite feather | *The healthy part of food that does you good | Kind and honest behaviour | A loud surprise
exercise: Maya drops her ice cream and cries, «My goodness!» What is goodness showing here? | Kindness to others | Hunger | Sadness | *Surprise
exercise: Find and copy the word that means the healthy part of food: «A panda gets little goodness from bamboo.» | *goodness | gets | panda | bamboo
test: Lena shares her last sweet with her little brother, and her mum says, «That was real goodness.» What does goodness mean here? | *Kind and honest behaviour | Healthy food in the fridge | Being very tired | Surprise
test: «Thank goodness the rain stopped before the match.» What does thank goodness show? | Confusion | *Relief | Anger | Boredom
exam: «My goodness, look at that rainbow!» What meaning fits best? | The healthy part of food | Kind and honest behaviour | *Surprise | A duck pond
